## GRACEFUL FALLBACK STRATEGY

All 5 tabs implement the same pattern:
  1. Attempt live connection (timeout=2-4s)
  2. If connection fails → show amber status badge + info banner
  3. Render demo/mock data so UI is never blank
  4. Mock data is domain-realistic (ZAR incomes, SA provinces, real field names)

Tabs that will show live data once services are running:
  - tab_tax_kpi.py    : Redis + MinIO/DuckDB (requires Sub-Tasks 2, 3, 4)
  - tab_fraud.py      : PostgreSQL + MinIO/DuckDB (requires Sub-Tasks 2, 3, 4)
  - tab_agent_chat.py : LangGraph agent (requires Sub-Task 7)
  - tab_lineage.py    : Marquez API (requires Sub-Task 8 Phase B)
  - tab_mlflow.py     : MLflow REST API (requires Sub-Task 6)

## PODMAN COMPOSE VALIDATION
NOTE: This project uses Podman, not Docker. All compose commands use `podman compose`.

Command to validate compose file:
  podman compose config

Command to build images and start full stack:
  podman compose up -d --build

Command to check streamlit container only (fastest test):
  podman compose up -d --build streamlit

Check container status:
  podman compose ps

Expected result: streamlit container healthy at http://localhost:8501

## KNOWN ENVIRONMENT NOTE
Podman binary not on automated PowerShell shell PATH.
Manual execution required from a terminal where Podman is on PATH (e.g. Podman Desktop terminal).
All file content correct and ready — no code errors detected via static review.

## PODMAN-SPECIFIC COMPATIBILITY NOTES
1. Makefile: Uses `podman compose` (built-in v4.7+) with fallback to `podman-compose`
2. Makefile: Uses `podman exec` (not `docker exec`) for container exec calls
3. scripts/submit_flink_jobs.py (Sub-Task 3): Must use `podman exec flink-sql-client ...`
4. Rootless Podman: containers run without root — all port bindings below 1024 require
   sysctl net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=0 (not applicable here — all ports are 3000+)
5. Volume mounts: Podman rootless may require :Z SELinux label on Linux.
   On Windows/Mac with Podman Desktop this is NOT needed.
